Areas for Improvement
Keyword Optimization:

While your meta description and title tag include relevant keywords, the body content could use more targeted keywords. For example:
In the About Me section, you could emphasize phrases like "custom web development solutions" or "digital marketing strategies" more explicitly.
In the Services section, ensure that each service description includes relevant keywords (e.g., "responsive web design," "SEO services").
Heading Hierarchy:

Ensure proper use of heading tags (<h1>, <h2>, <h3>) for better structure:
Currently, there is no <h1> tag. The <h1> tag should ideally be the main title of the page (e.g., "Mark Soliz - Full-Stack Developer").
Use <h2> for major sections (e.g., "About Me," "Services") and <h3> for subsections (e.g., individual services like "Web Development").
Image Optimization:

While you have alt attributes, consider optimizing image filenames and alt text with keywords. For example:
Rename me.jpg to something like mark-soliz-full-stack-developer.jpg.
Update the alt text to something like Mark Soliz - Full-Stack Developer Profile Picture.
Content Readability:

Break up longer paragraphs in the About Me section for better readability. Search engines favor content that is easy to read and scannable.
Missing Keywords in Footer Links:

The footer links (e.g., "Home," "About," "Portfolio") could include more descriptive anchor text. For example:
Instead of "About," use "About Mark Soliz - Full-Stack Developer."
Schema Markup:

Add structured data (e.g., JSON-LD) to help search engines better understand your content. For example, you can use schema for:
Person: To highlight your name, profession, and contact details.
Organization: If you want to emphasize your business.
Breadcrumbs: To improve navigation.
Page Speed Optimization:

Ensure that your images are optimized for faster loading. Use tools like TinyPNG to compress images without losing quality.
Social Media Meta Tags:

Add Open Graph (OG) and Twitter Card meta tags to improve how your site appears when shared on social media. For example:

<meta property="og:title" content="Mark Soliz - Full-Stack Developer">
<meta property="og:description" content="Specializing in web development, web hosting, and digital marketing. Helping businesses succeed with tailored solutions.">
<meta property="og:image" content="./assets/images/me.jpg">
<meta property="og:url" content="https://marksoliz.com">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">

